cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AutoBarcoder: 96-well plate RNA barcode demultiplexing and clustering"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bachu
    given-names: Abhinav
repository-code: "https://github.com/abachu2005/AutoBarcoder-OS-"
url: "https://github.com/abachu2005/AutoBarcoder-OS-"
abstract: >-
  AutoBarcoder is a Python tool for demultiplexing and clustering RNA
  barcodes from 96-well-plate sequencing reads. It uses Levenshtein
  distance and a connected-components graph (NetworkX) to group similar
  barcodes per well and outputs per-well summaries (TXT + PDF) plus an
  interactive web frontend.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - sequencing
  - barcode-analysis
  - 96-well-plate
  - clustering
  - RNA
license: MIT
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-05-19"
